1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,575
Today, every time you say sorry, the

2
00:00:03,595 --> 00:00:06,095
other person forgets what you did.

3
00:00:06,285 --> 00:00:07,465
Not forgives.

4
00:00:07,485 --> 00:00:08,480
Forgets.

5
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:10,505
You break your brother's controller.

6
00:00:10,525 --> 00:00:11,776
Sorry, Theo.

7
00:00:12,576 --> 00:00:13,913
Sorry for what?

8
00:00:14,663 --> 00:00:16,554
It's the best day of your life.

9
00:00:17,244 --> 00:00:18,647
For about a week.

10
00:00:21,697 --> 00:00:23,477
Theo moved in on Monday.

11
00:00:23,497 --> 00:00:24,652
Temporarily.

12
00:00:24,672 --> 00:00:26,952
With four bags, a games console, and

13
00:00:26,972 --> 00:00:27,961
no plan.

14
00:00:28,951 --> 00:00:31,305
On Tuesday, you're twenty minutes late.

15
00:00:31,325 --> 00:00:32,361
Twenty minutes.

16
00:00:32,381 --> 00:00:33,091
Again.

17
00:00:33,111 --> 00:00:34,483
Do you know what time

18
00:00:34,503 --> 00:00:35,391
Sorry.

19
00:00:36,191 --> 00:00:37,406
Ah, good morning!

20
00:00:37,426 --> 00:00:39,046
Early, as always.

21
00:00:40,096 --> 00:00:42,176
You forget your wallet at the café.

22
00:00:42,196 --> 00:00:43,815
Third time this month.

23
00:00:43,835 --> 00:00:44,485
Sorry.

24
00:00:44,505 --> 00:00:45,953
I'll pay you tomorrow.

25
00:00:45,973 --> 00:00:47,129
Pay me for what?

26
00:00:47,279 --> 00:00:48,384
Free coffee.

27
00:00:48,404 --> 00:00:50,009
You decide not to think about it too

28
00:00:50,029 --> 00:00:50,791
hard.

29
00:00:51,781 --> 00:00:53,875
You knock over a stranger's scooter.

30
00:00:53,895 --> 00:00:54,425
Oh no.

31
00:00:54,445 --> 00:00:55,320
Sorry!

32
00:00:56,120 --> 00:00:57,243
What scooter?

33
00:00:57,393 --> 00:00:59,648
By Tuesday night, you've said sorry

34
00:00:59,668 --> 00:01:01,883
eleven times, and you've been in trouble

35
00:01:01,903 --> 00:01:03,103
zero.

36
00:01:03,393 --> 00:01:05,423
You don't notice the little grey smudge

37
00:01:05,443 --> 00:01:07,663
it leaves over everyone's head.

38
00:01:07,683 --> 00:01:08,497
Not yet.

39
00:01:10,146 --> 00:01:12,326
On Wednesday, Theo plays until two in

40
00:01:12,346 --> 00:01:13,267
the morning.

41
00:01:13,287 --> 00:01:13,887
Theo.

42
00:01:13,907 --> 00:01:15,475
It's two a.m.

43
00:01:15,495 --> 00:01:16,878
Five more minutes.

44
00:01:17,028 --> 00:01:18,908
And you say the thing you've been thinking

45
00:01:18,928 --> 00:01:19,911
since Monday.

46
00:01:19,931 --> 00:01:22,436
You know why nobody lets you stay anywhere?

47
00:01:22,456 --> 00:01:23,916
Because you're exhausting.

48
00:01:26,246 --> 00:01:27,134
Sorry.

49
00:01:27,934 --> 00:01:29,271
Sorry for what?

50
00:01:29,921 --> 00:01:31,276
He doesn't remember.

51
00:01:31,296 --> 00:01:33,026
But he doesn't pick the controller back

52
00:01:33,046 --> 00:01:33,931
up either.

53
00:01:34,921 --> 00:01:36,866
The next morning, he's quiet.

54
00:01:36,886 --> 00:01:38,266
He washes your mug.

55
00:01:38,286 --> 00:01:40,074
He asks if he's in the way.

56
00:01:40,094 --> 00:01:41,099
Did I do something?

57
00:01:41,119 --> 00:01:42,168
You can tell me.

58
00:01:42,188 --> 00:01:42,543
No.

59
00:01:42,563 --> 00:01:43,780
You didn't do anything.

60
00:01:43,930 --> 00:01:45,080
That's the problem.

61
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:45,825
He didn't.

62
00:01:45,845 --> 00:01:46,810
You did.

63
00:01:46,830 --> 00:01:48,408
And he's the one carrying it.

64
00:01:49,398 --> 00:01:51,628
Now you see the smudges everywhere.

65
00:01:51,648 --> 00:01:52,903
Over your boss.

66
00:01:52,923 --> 00:01:54,623
Over the barista.

67
00:01:54,643 --> 00:01:56,998
Small grey clouds where a memory used

68
00:01:57,018 --> 00:01:57,706
to be.

69
00:01:58,616 --> 00:01:59,466
Weird week.

70
00:01:59,506 --> 00:02:01,111
I keep feeling annoyed at someone, and

71
00:02:01,131 --> 00:02:02,491
I can't remember who.

72
00:02:02,511 --> 00:02:03,478
That's weird.

73
00:02:03,498 --> 00:02:04,353
You want your usual?

74
00:02:04,373 --> 00:02:05,578
It's on Actually.

75
00:02:05,598 --> 00:02:07,252
Have you paid me lately?

76
00:02:07,402 --> 00:02:08,757
The memory goes.

77
00:02:08,777 --> 00:02:10,387
The feeling stays.

78
00:02:10,407 --> 00:02:12,399
And nobody knows where it came from.

79
00:02:14,349 --> 00:02:17,425
Then, on Friday, you forget Mira's birthday.

80
00:02:17,445 --> 00:02:17,700
Hey.

81
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:18,220
So.

82
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:19,516
It's ten p.m.

83
00:02:20,266 --> 00:02:21,601
The word is right there.

84
00:02:21,621 --> 00:02:22,276
Sorry.

85
00:02:22,296 --> 00:02:24,164
One word, and she'll never know.

86
00:02:24,754 --> 00:02:26,684
And she'll still go to bed sad, and

87
00:02:26,704 --> 00:02:27,903
not know why.

88
00:02:28,813 --> 00:02:29,508
Mira.

89
00:02:29,528 --> 00:02:31,058
I forgot your birthday.

90
00:02:31,078 --> 00:02:32,353
Completely.

91
00:02:32,388 --> 00:02:34,243
And I'm not going to say the word, because

92
00:02:34,263 --> 00:02:35,932
I want you to stay mad at me.

93
00:02:35,952 --> 00:02:37,882
That is the weirdest apology I have

94
00:02:37,902 --> 00:02:38,637
ever heard.

95
00:02:38,657 --> 00:02:40,087
It's not an apology.

96
00:02:40,107 --> 00:02:41,327
It's a confession.

97
00:02:41,347 --> 00:02:41,947
Fine.

98
00:02:41,987 --> 00:02:42,692
I'm mad.

99
00:02:42,712 --> 00:02:43,697
You owe me a cake.

100
00:02:43,717 --> 00:02:44,505
A big one.

101
00:02:45,134 --> 00:02:45,844
Okay.

102
00:02:45,864 --> 00:02:46,886
I'm a bit less mad.

103
00:02:46,906 --> 00:02:47,656
Saturday.

104
00:02:47,676 --> 00:02:48,246
Cake.

105
00:02:48,266 --> 00:02:49,193
In person.

106
00:02:49,213 --> 00:02:50,767
It's four hours on a train.

107
00:02:50,787 --> 00:02:53,002
It's going to be a very big cake.

108
00:02:53,152 --> 00:02:54,132
No shimmer.

109
00:02:54,152 --> 00:02:55,282
No smudge.

110
00:02:55,302 --> 00:02:57,572
Just Mira, remembering, and forgiving

111
00:02:57,592 --> 00:02:58,823
you anyway.

112
00:02:58,843 --> 00:03:00,773
It's the first time all week anyone

113
00:03:00,793 --> 00:03:01,544
has.

114
00:03:02,534 --> 00:03:04,738
Then you go and sit next to Theo.

115
00:03:04,758 --> 00:03:06,714
On Wednesday, I said something horrible

116
00:03:06,734 --> 00:03:07,289
to you.

117
00:03:07,309 --> 00:03:08,514
You don't remember it.

118
00:03:08,534 --> 00:03:09,182
I do.

119
00:03:09,202 --> 00:03:10,436
What did you say?

120
00:03:10,585 --> 00:03:11,475
You tell him.

121
00:03:11,495 --> 00:03:12,704
Word for word.

122
00:03:13,414 --> 00:03:13,719
Wow.

123
00:03:13,739 --> 00:03:14,695
That's rude.

124
00:03:14,715 --> 00:03:15,355
Yeah.

125
00:03:15,375 --> 00:03:17,082
I am a bit exhausting, though.

126
00:03:17,102 --> 00:03:18,507
You're a lot exhausting.

127
00:03:18,527 --> 00:03:19,757
Stay anyway.

128
00:03:21,407 --> 00:03:23,687
The grey smudge over his head fades,

129
00:03:23,707 --> 00:03:25,339
like breath on a window.

130
00:03:25,359 --> 00:03:27,198
Can I have your controller, then?

131
00:03:27,218 --> 00:03:27,999
No.

132
00:03:29,049 --> 00:03:31,444
On Saturday, you carry a very large

133
00:03:31,464 --> 00:03:33,483
cake for four hours.

134
00:03:33,503 --> 00:03:35,548
Mira eats a third of it on a bench,

135
00:03:35,568 --> 00:03:37,273
and tells you she's still a little bit

136
00:03:37,293 --> 00:03:38,262
mad.

137
00:03:38,282 --> 00:03:39,426
You let her be.

138
00:03:41,817 --> 00:03:44,479
Would you rather be forgiven, or forgotten?
